 "final_message": "The application (BHL-26001) is submitted, and I've recorded your intent to proceed on the Loan Estimate. The lender's condition about business accounts is still unmet, though. The status page shows the condition as \"response received.\"\n\n- **Application:** I submitted it once, with the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts and the last 2 payslips for each of you. I also gave the credit-check and e-sign consents.\n- **Loan Estimate:** It is within all your limits.\n\n| | Loan Estimate | Your limit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rate | 6.25% | 6.5% |\n| Monthly payment | $3,042.41 | $3,100 |\n| Closing costs | $12,850 | $14,000 |\n\n- **Underwriting condition:** I explained that the $8,000 deposit on 09/03 was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment and isn't a loan. The lender also asked for statements on all accounts, including business accounts. I told them you're applying on personal income and accounts only, so I sent nothing from Nadia's business account, as you asked.\n- **Possible follow-up:** The lender may press for the business statements, and I have no way to tell from here whether this response satisfies them.",
